Own the end-to-end technical performance of a portfolio of strategic accounts across Latin America and Africa, focusing on approval rates, chargebacks, refunds, payouts, latency, and Share of Wallet growth;
Investigate payment performance changes and identify their root causes, including issuer behavior, decline-code mapping, 3DS authentication failures, retry logic, acquirer routing, and network-tokenization gaps;
Use SQL and data-analysis tools to turn large volumes of payment data into clear, actionable recommendations for merchants and internal stakeholders;
Collaborate with Product and Engineering teams to design A/B tests for payment flows, evaluate their results, and recommend decisions based on performance;
Lead technical workstreams for new-market, payment-method, and integration launches;
Partner with Risk to reduce chargebacks through migration initiatives, rule adjustments, and payment-flow redesigns;
Lead technical discussions during QBRs and executive reviews, translating complex technical findings into business impact and recommendations for VP and C-level stakeholders;
Coordinate incident response, maintaining clear communication with merchants while issues are still under investigation and preparing post-incident analyses;
Identify, assess, and size account-expansion opportunities, including new countries, payment methods, and business units within existing merchants;
Mentor Analyst and Junior TAMs, reviewing their analyses and supporting complex escalations.
What you need to shine in this role
Strong experience in technical account management, solutions engineering, payments operations, or another client-facing technical role;
A curious and investigative mindset, with the initiative to explore data, challenge assumptions, and continue digging until the actual cause of an issue is identified;
Good working knowledge of SQL and the ability to query and analyze large datasets with autonomy; experience with BigQuery is a plus;
Working knowledge of the payments ecosystem, including authorization flows, acquiring, issuing, 3DS, tokenization, chargebacks, settlement, REST APIs, and webhooks;
Fluency in English and Portuguese, with the ability to communicate clearly with global stakeholders;
Ability to navigate effectively between technical and commercial audiences, translating engineering topics into clear business implications and recommendations;
Comfort working with incomplete information, managing ambiguity, and driving investigations forward;
Experience using AI tools to accelerate data investigation and documentation, combined with sound judgment about when outputs require further validation.

Experience using Python for data analysis, including pandas or equivalent libraries;
Fluency or professional proficiency in Spanish;
Experience working with global merchants in industries such as streaming, marketplaces, gaming, travel, SaaS, or subscriptions;
Exposure to card-network programs, including network tokens, Visa and Mastercard credential-on-file programs, and account updater services;
Experience with local payment methods across Latin America or Africa;
Familiarity with BI and observability tools such as Tableau, Looker, OpenSearch, Datadog, or similar platforms;
Previous experience mentoring others or leading initiatives without formal authority.

